.archon-horizon/inbox/local/comments/I-0322/C-0001.md:24:WHY I MOVED IT INSTEAD OF DELETING IT, which this item authorised. Its Hartshorne quotes were transcribed character-by-character from rendered page images of a scanned PDF with no text layer (pages 62, 314, 316), and references/hartshorne-algebraic-geometry/pages/ currently holds only three page images (0154, 0155, 0316) and no transcription of them. Deleting the file would destroy transcription work that is not mirrored anywhere. The header says: harvest into references/ first, then delete.
